From d38826f03cdfe374ab0ed00c1cf026a4437b3040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Air battle sound: real B-17s replace the studio library's
 (Brian's Goods, round nine)

Brian stamped round nine on the listening page at 03:40-03:41Z on 22 Nov: both
recordings from inside a B-17, the formation flying over, and the fly-away all
Good. This wires the first three; the fly-away waits for the far battle bed,
which is a new mix and goes to his ear first.

Riding a B-17 plays one of two recordings from inside one, picked by the
bomber's key, so two B-17s ridden in turn sound like two aircraft:
b17_interior_whiteman_loop (Wings Over Whiteman, 2017) and
b17_interior_sioux_loop (the Commemorative Air Force's B-17 at Sioux City,
2022). air.closeView.bed.interior now takes a take or a list; a take not yet
built into the game gives way to the next, and none keeps the filtered drone.

A B-17 formation's engines are b17_formation_drone_loop: three B-17s and five
P-51s flying over, filmed from the ground (air.loops B-17).

All three are U.S. Air Force video on DVIDS (public domain), credited in
credits.json and CREDITS.md. All are mono 48 kHz 16-bit at -20.0 LUFS, the
loudness of the takes they replace, so interiorGainDb stays 2. The old
craigsmith takes (b17_interior_loop, b17_drone_loop) stay in the folder,
no longer played; G07-18 still plays inside air_battle_far_loop until the far
bed is rebuilt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
